{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":31,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The final network brings dev TTS from 48.0 to **45.4 veh-h**, against 44.7 with every detector working. `work/weights.npz`, `work/NOTES.md` and `work/predictions.json` are written, along with all scripts.\n\n**What I changed and why**\n- **Reading W2 from E2 (128 parameters):** E and W have the same demand and their left-turn pockets get green together, so the network now treats the dead W2 inputs as equal to the E2 readings. I added the W2 weights onto the E2 weights. Without this, phase 3 was never picked while the E pocket was empty.\n- **Breaking stalls (171 parameters):** with an almost empty junction the network holds phase 2 forever. It never serves a lone N/S through car, which is a flaw it had before the fault, or a lone W-left car, which is now invisible. Such cars waited until the 30-minute drain cap. I reused the least important first-layer unit (57) as a \"phase 2 held ≥ 60 s\" detector. Its second-layer weights make the network act as if it saw two W-left cars plus about one extra car per N/S through lane.\n\n**Parameters changed:** 299 of the 371 allowed.\n\n**Simulator calls:** 7 of 10.\n- Call 1 (W2 from E2 only): 45.6, with 5 cars stuck at the cap.\n- Calls 2–3 (time-based ramps): no better.\n- Call 4 (delivered): 45.4, with 0 cars stuck.\n- Calls 5–7 (a W1u spillback term and two ways of shrinking the E2 estimate): 45.4–45.5, within noise.\n\n**Delivered dev TTS:** 45.4 (low 35.0, nominal 45.6, high 55.7).\n\n**Test predictions:** low 35.1, nominal 45.7, high 56.0.","ttft_ms":6260,"type":"result","duration_ms":966098,"uuid":"e33394d9-ad9d-43f4-adeb-28826bd559a7","ttft_stream_ms":5723,"time_to_request_ms":61,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":3,"system_prompt":7,"resume_other":1,"process_user_input":1,"input_attachments":12,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":5,"tool_pool_refresh":3,"init_message":3,"init_frame_send"